      "writtenOn": "2015-05-28T02:09:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We discussed this with Randall before. We suggest two solutions to place header structure. One is containing header in RO region and the other is treating header as individual region. We thought first one is better with existing workflow. If flashrom tries to write RO code, it is more complicated. For example, we need to make sure erasing header at the same time. \nCurrently, CONFIG_CODERAM_ARCH is only used by npcx chip and the booter in ROM restricts the header must locate in the front of FW which is copied from flash to CODE RAM. It was mentioned in the NPCX5M5G ROM code datasheet released a few months ago.",
      "parentUuid": "adfdb1c1_ffa3dfff",
      "revId": "b68eb95457dcef4bc55119ef37e4a3e5a2a6bab4",
