      "message": "Changing line 101 from \"#ifdef CONFIG_CODERAM_ARCH\" to \"#ifdef CONFIG_FW_HEADER_SIZE\" is better or not? I agree CONFIG_CODERAM_ARCH is not good choice for further architecture. But treating header as a part of RO is more simple. For example, I didn\u0027t change firmware_image.lds.S to put the header into ec.bin. Once RO contains header, we need to consider the length of header to get correct offset.",
